          {
            "label": "Additional Metadata Filter",
            "name": "retrieverToolMetadataFilter",
            "type": "json",
            "description": "Add additional metadata filter on top of the existing filter from vector store",
            "optional": true,
            "additionalParams": true,
            "hint": {
              "label": "What can you filter?",
              "value": "Add additional filters to vector store. You can also filter with flow config, including the current \"state\":\n- `$flow.sessionId`\n- `$flow.chatId`\n- `$flow.chatflowId`\n- `$flow.input`\n- `$flow.state`\n"
            },
            "acceptVariable": true,
            "id": "retrieverTool_0-input-retrieverToolMetadataFilter-json",
            "display": true
          }
        ],
        "inputAnchors": [
          {
            "label": "Retriever",
            "name": "retriever",
            "type": "BaseRetriever",
            "id": "retrieverTool_0-input-retriever-BaseRetriever",
            "display": true
          }
        ],
        "inputs": {
          "name": "policy_checker",
          "description": "This tool retrieves procurement policy rules, thresholds, and governance clauses from the source policy PDF.\n\nUse this tool for:\n- Disruption response levels and activation criteria (Level 1, 2, 3)\n- Supplier Watch List (SWL) criteria, compliance score thresholds, and new PO restrictions\n- Volume Rebate Program eligibility criteria and qualification conditions\n- Regional concentration limits and breach consequences\n- Defect rate thresholds by tier (Tier-1, Tier-2, Tier-3)\n- Escalation procedures and timelines\n- Alternate supplier activation requirements\n- Any policy rule, threshold, percentage cap, or program condition\n\nSearch queries to use for each topic:\n- Disruption response: query \"disruption response level High Risk Tier-3 activation\"\n- Watch List restrictions: query \"Supplier Watch List SWL compliance score new PO restriction\"\n- Volume Rebate: query \"Volume Rebate Program eligibility criteria qualification\"\n- Regional concentration: query \"regional concentration limit spend cap percentage breach\"\n- Defect rate thresholds: query \"defect rate Tier-2 Tier-3 threshold limit\"\n\nInstructions:\n- Treat retrieved text as the ONLY source of truth for policy rules.\n- Return the EXACT threshold, percentage, timeline, or condition from the retrieved text.\n- Do NOT paraphrase vaguely. Give the specific number (e.g. '20% of prior-quarter volume', '45% cap', 'score below 60', '2.50 defect rate', 'Level 3 Activate').\n- If a rule is not found in retrieved text, say: 'I could not confirm that rule from the retrieved policy text.'\n- Do NOT infer or assume policy language not present in the retrieved chunks.\n- Quote or summarize the retrieved rule faithfully without adding new conditions.\n- Always return the policy rule BEFORE the SQL query is interpreted, so the correct filter can be applied.",
          "retriever": "{{documentStoreVS_0.data.instance}}",
          "returnSourceDocuments": "",
          "retrieverToolMetadataFilter": ""
        },
        "outputAnchors": [
          {
            "id": "retrieverTool_0-output-retrieverTool-RetrieverTool|DynamicTool|Tool|StructuredTool|Runnable",
            "name": "retrieverTool",
            "label": "RetrieverTool",
            "description": "Use a retriever as allowed tool for agent",
            "type": "RetrieverTool | DynamicTool | Tool | StructuredTool | Runnable"
          }
        ],
